{
 "name": "locked_antlers_ice",
 "description": "Two bull moose antler racks locked together and sticking up through flat ice (Unalakleet 2016): each rack is a pair of broad pale palmate paddles (#d9c49a, same shape as moose_antler_rack) with tines along the rims, on a short bone stub at the ice. The inner paddles overlap in the middle; the front (left) rack's tines lie over the back rack's paddle and two back-rack tines hook over the front, so they read as interlocked. Snow on the tine tips, broken ice rims and cracks around the bases. No heads, no bodies, nothing below the ice line. Anchor (0,0) = ice surface at the centre; x -350..350, y -260..0.",
